From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:47:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: Build the GenUI-min configuration and report its size

GenUI-min is the smallest servoshell configuration for generated pages
on OpenHarmony that the size measurements of 2026-10-12 settled on
(stack G2 plus RELR and ICF there). A justfile at the top level keeps
its flags in one place: `just genui-min` builds it and its HAP with
`./mach build`, and `just genui-min-size` prints the size of the
stripped library and of the HAP.

- QuickJS, the OpenHarmony RDB storage backend, and
  `--no-default-features` with only bundled, max_log_level and
  servo/clipboard: no WebGPU, WebGL, WebXR, WebCrypto (and so no `crypto`
  global), gamepad, brotli in CompressionStream, multiprocess, devtools
  or jemalloc. RDB instead of SQLite saves only 16 KB for now, because
  components/net links rusqlite for its disk cache in any case, but it
  makes this the build in CI that covers the RDB backend.
- A `genui-min` Cargo profile, defined with `--config`: `production` at
  opt-level "z" and with panic=abort. It has its own output directory,
  so a production build in the same target directory stays intact.
- RELR relocations and `--icf=all` through RUSTFLAGS, which mach
  appends to. Cargo ignores `target.<triple>.rustflags` whenever
  RUSTFLAGS is set, and mach always sets it.

The new GenUI-min workflow runs the recipes, writes the sizes to the job
summary and uploads the HAP and the unstripped library. A second job
sends both sizes to the servo-ohos project on Bencher, with a project
key in the BENCHER_API_KEY secret of the bencher environment, which only
that job uses: pushes to ohos-main to its ohos-main branch, and pull
requests from this repository to a `<number>/PR` branch that starts at
the base commit and takes over its thresholds, with a comment on the
pull request. Main passes the secret on, because a reusable workflow
only gets the environment secrets that its caller passes. The Bencher
jobs inherited from Servo use BENCHER_API_TOKEN and stay off. The Main
workflow calls it for pull requests that need the OpenHarmony or
QuickJS build; it also runs on pushes to ohos-main and on demand. It
doesn't decide the result of Main.

The build runs on the self-hosted runners labelled servo-ohos-linux,
whose image needs the OpenHarmony SDK, hvigor, just and a prebuilt
target directory of this build for that. Pull requests from forks and
runs while NO_SELF_HOSTED_RUNNERS is set build on a GitHub-hosted
runner, set up as for the OpenHarmony build, with an unsigned HAP.

pr_jobs counts the justfile and the workflow as OpenHarmony-only files,
so that a pull request changing them runs GenUI-min.

The justfile is force-added: upstream's .gitignore lists `justfile` so
that developers can keep a personal one at the top level, and such a
file now blocks checking out this branch until it is renamed.

Left out for now: static libc++ (HAP -0.83 MiB, needs a packaging
change), the exported-symbols list (about 0 for QuickJS), and the
source changes measured with this stack (servoshell without testbinding
and bluetooth, capitalize without the CJ dictionary).

Validation: `just genui-min` on ohos-main 013edabb25d, in a fresh target directory on 32 cores, built in 4 min 7 s with the OpenHarmony 6.1 SDK as cargo-ohos installs it (`cargo ohos init sdk --version 6.1`, what the runner image will use); a change to storage's features rebuilt storage, servo and servoshell in 2 min 17 s. The library is 29,387,176 bytes after llvm-strip (28.03 MiB), with `.relr.dyn` and a 3.6 KB `.rela.dyn` (RELR on), a 13.8 KB `.gcc_except_table` (panic=abort) and NEEDED libnative_rdb_ndk.z.so; the same build with sqlite-backend was 16,128 B larger and both link 290 sqlite3_ symbols. That fits the 2026-10-12 stack: its 26.14 MiB included static libc++ (+0.44 on the library) and the two source changes (-1.02 and -1.92), which this patch leaves out, so about 28.6 MiB here, less devtools (about -0.5, not yet a feature on that base) and plus the code merged since. hvigor 5 from npm packaged the default-flavor HAP against that SDK (34,205,612 B unsigned, the library in it byte-for-byte the llvm-strip size), and `just genui-min-size` printed both sizes. `bencher run --dry-run` (CLI 0.6.13), run outside a checkout with the Bencher job's script and this build's sizes, reports both as file-size benchmarks: for a push on ohos-main at GITHUB_SHA, for a pull request on 42/PR at the head commit with the start point ohos-main at the base commit (reset, thresholds cloned). On GitHub, a run on pull request 38 built GenUI-min and reached the Bencher job, which got an empty key before Main passed the secret on; the upload itself has not run there yet. pr_jobs tests pass (12), `./mach test-tidy` passes, and actionlint 1.7 reports nothing new (the missing action-metadata descriptions and the decision step's SC2086 exist on ohos-main). Not run: the workflow on GitHub, and a self-hosted runner image with the OpenHarmony toolchain (prepared separately in ohos-ci-runners); this build was not run on a device.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, which also built and packaged the configuration locally)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 .github/workflows/main.yml           |  15 +++
 .github/workflows/ohos-genui-min.yml | 144 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 justfile                             |  36 +++++++
 python/servo/pr_jobs.py              |   2 +
 4 files changed, 197 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 .github/workflows/ohos-genui-min.yml
 create mode 100644 justfile

diff --git a/.github/workflows/main.yml b/.github/workflows/main.yml
index ae1a88f16be..b6ebc510566 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/main.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/main.yml
@@ -83,6 +83,21 @@ jobs:
       coverage: ${{ matrix.coverage }}
       capi: ${{ matrix.capi }}
 
+  # Pull requests that need the OpenHarmony or QuickJS build also build GenUI-min, which doesn't
+  # decide the result.
+  genui-min:
+    name: GenUI-min
+    needs: ["decision"]
+    if: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && (contains(fromJson(needs.decision.outputs.configuration).matrix.*.workflow, 'ohos') || contains(fromJson(needs.decision.outputs.configuration).matrix.*.workflow, 'quickjs')) }}
+    permissions:
